ly via a catch-all '/ Full' rule (excluding /proc, /sys) plus curated per-package rules, and added an explicit '/etc Full' fragment for clarity. Built and installed the baseline database at /var/lib/aide/aide.db (70,163 entries) with creation timestamp and sha256 recorded under /var/lib/aide/baseline-meta/. Verified change detection by creating a test file under /etc, confirming aide --check flagged it as added, then removing it and confirming a clean state. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id and healthy baseline state, issued a native reboot, polled until SSH returned, proved boot_id changed, and confirmed post-restart that the baseline database was byte-identical (same sha256), /etc still matched the baseline, and change detection still worked correctly.","actions_performed":["Installed aide and aide-common via apt on node1","Inspected AIDE's default Debian/Ubuntu config and confirmed /etc is covered by a catch-all '/ Full' rule plus curated per-package rules","Added /etc/aide/aide.conf.d/50-etc-full-baseline.conf with an explicit '/etc Full' recursive rule","Ran aideinit to build the baseline database and promoted aide.db.new to the active aide.db","Recorded baseline metadata (creation timestamp and sha256 of aide.db) under /var/lib/aide/baseline-meta/","Verified detection by creating /etc/aide-baseline-test.conf, confirming aide --check flagged it as added, then removing it","Captured pre-restart boot_id and confirmed baseline health with zero /etc diffs","Issued a native reboot (shutdown -r now) on node1; acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until SSH access returned and confirmed boot_id changed, proving an actual restart","Post-restart, verified aide.db sha256 was unchanged, /etc still showed zero diffs against baseline, and change detection still worked (new /etc file flagged, then cleaned up)"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Integrity baseline established for /etc","command_ids":["cmd-6f7dfba